1) Unprocessable Records
known as Poison Pill Messages, will stop the application, require manual intervention.


two types of error: 
Transcient errors-temporary, will eventually recover automatically.
Non- transcient Error- not temporary, wil not recover by themselves. 


DEAD LETTER PATTERN
- identify where the code fails: custom mapping function, error-safe transformation. 
- apply safety controlsL try-catch block. 
- include the failed messages as the metadata  (Metadata Decorator pattern)
- configure a different output for the erroneous events. (Dead letter storage) 

Consequences
1) Snowball backfilling effect
consumer will continue to ingest partial data
backfilling on upstream does not guarantee downstream pipeline will be re-run

2) Dead-lettered records identification
might need to identified whether this was dead lettered, add another column 'was_dead_lettered'

3) Ordering & consistency
-ordered might be messed up if data backfilling is re-run

4) Error safe functions
-reduced the risk of run time issue, not throw erro but return NULL value, might not be able to catch error hence missed an unprocessed record if it returns NULL. 


2) Duplicated Records

WINDOWED DECUPLICATOR
1) Identify Deduplication attributes
2) Define deduplication scope
Batch job: currently processed dataset
Streaming Job: create time-based windows.

Take note of space vs time trade off
- time window too short , might miss some duplicates, longer windows, takes up resources
